From 023f5f10a4a4a6188107dfbc8106fa62e72c74be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:08:19 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 05/22] feat(reframe): find a streamer's facecam window from
 its border

The face-first reactor check needs a face in most samples, in an upper
corner, with another face lower down. Real streams miss all three: the
facecam face is ~16 px after the analysis downscale, cameras float
half-way down a side, and gameplay rarely shows faces (Kai Cenat 1080p:
face found in 6/121 samples).

facecam_rect finds the camera window instead: per-pixel median Sobel
edges over ~10 frames, side-anchored rectangles of plausible size and
aspect (overlapping candidates collapsed), a YuNet face on the
full-resolution crop in >= 40 % of frames, and no second camera-sized
face fixed elsewhere (video calls, Omegle splits). The EDL planner
delegates such clips to the plain path, where choose_reaction_layout
falls back to the window when the face-first check misses; the
reaction layout now handles insets that do not touch the top
(inset_bottom; identical for top-anchored insets).

Real-video check (30 windows, 15 videos): 14/16 streamer facecams,
2/2 lecture presenter windows, 0 false positives on podcast, vlog,
comedy, talking head and both iShowSpeed layouts. Misses: Kai looking
down at his desk. FACECAM_RECT_DETECT=0 switches it off.

Also adds media/gaming_templates.py (face-on-top stack renderer, wired
in the next commit) and a Gaming HD entry in the Phase 2 runner.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
