 ## 2026-11-17
+- **Improved:** Streamer clips now find the facecam even when it sits half-way down the side of the screen or the face is small, and even when the game shows no faces. The app looks for the camera window itself, checks there is a face in it, and then puts the streamer on top and the game below. It ignores video calls (several people in fixed windows) and stream overlays with a printed face. Set `FACECAM_RECT_DETECT=0` to switch this off.
 - **Fixed:** Video-call podcasts (each person in their own window) sometimes came out as the whole call shrunk into the middle of the vertical frame, with small faces. A still face in a top corner was being mistaken for a streamer's facecam. Now a facecam also needs a camera frame the app can actually measure; otherwise the clip gets the normal layout, which shows both people large, one above the other. Set `REFRAME_REACTOR_NEEDS_INSET=0` to restore the previous check.
 - **Fixed:** On a computer with an NVIDIA graphics card but without the CUDA libraries installed (common outside the Docker image), transcription crashed or hung. It now switches to the processor once and remembers that for the rest of the run. `WHISPER_DEVICE=cpu` forces the processor.
 - **Improved:** Clip quality checks can now flag a clip that is far from the -14 LUFS loudness short-form platforms use, and a clip that opens or ends mid-sentence or cuts a word. Both are warnings only and run when the pipeline supplies the loudness target and transcript.
